__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
data/raw/
data/processed/
data/cache/
logs/
*.egg-info/
.DS_Store

# Small built artefacts the site workflow needs (the 113 MB river network lives in a release)
!data/processed/
data/processed/*
!data/processed/annual_returns.parquet
!data/processed/id_lookup.parquet
!data/processed/lakes.parquet
!data/processed/spill_model.pkl
!data/processed/spill_model_holdout_2025.pkl
# PR #254's live-status candidates, run in shadow only (model/live_status.py, docs/LIVE-STATUS-SHADOW-TEST-2026-10.md)
!data/processed/live_status/
# The regional routing shadow's frozen v2 model (shadow_regional.py, docs/REGIONAL-ROUTING-2026-11.md)
!data/processed/regional/
!data/processed/lead_calibration.json
!data/processed/spill_day_ratio.json
!data/processed/ecoli_model.json
!data/processed/ecoli_model_sm.json
!data/processed/ecoli_model_eval.json
!data/processed/water_temp_model.json
!data/processed/verification_2025.csv
!data/processed/reliability_2025.csv
!data/processed/verification_leads_2025.csv
!data/processed/ecoli_validation.json
!data/processed/ecoli_validation_combined.json
!data/processed/ecoli_validation_per_site.csv
!data/processed/validation_sites.csv
!data/processed/prf_comparison.json
!data/processed/sampling_plan_test.json
# Live scores withdrawn when the coverage rule changed, kept because README and the Method page cite them.
!data/processed/verification_live_oldrule_2026-09-28.json
# Scottish covariates (Scotland plan S2). Contains Scottish Water data licensed under the Open Government Licence v3.0.
!data/processed/sw_covariates.parquet
# Each overflow's longest spill in the EA's 2024-2025 start/stop records, for the data-quality page's long_run
# list (scripts/make_longest_events.py, 154 KB). Contains Environment Agency data, Open Government Licence v3.0.
!data/processed/longest_events.parquet
# Each overflow's permit and improvement activity from the annual returns (279 KB), and the WINEP's storm overflow
# improvement deadlines (77 KB), for the overflow record pages (scripts/make_overflow_record.py). Environment Agency
# data, Open Government Licence v3.0.
!data/processed/overflow_record.parquet
!data/processed/winep_overflow_actions.parquet
!data/raw/
data/raw/*
!data/raw/bathing_waters_inland.json
!data/raw/bathing_water_classifications.json
!data/raw/osm_swim_candidates.csv
!data/raw/wales_bathing_waters.json
!data/raw/coastal_catalogue.json
!data/raw/coastal_wqa_points.json
# Each English and Welsh bathing water's sampling point, for the directories' water temperature (scripts/refresh_bathing_water_points.py; OGL v3.0).
!data/raw/bathing_water_points.json
!data/raw/places.json
# The rivers and lakes the home page's search finds on the map (scripts/make_waters.py).
!data/raw/waters.json
!data/raw/outside_england.json
# Checked joins of outfalls on streams OS Open Rivers does not draw (overflows.apply_joins).
!data/raw/overflow_joins.csv
# Overflow upgrades their company has announced, with the page that says so: read by the page's note only, never the model (build_site.attach_upgrades).
!data/raw/overflow_upgrades.csv
# Fixes to the river network that the load-time rules do not make (dipcast.network.fixes).
!data/raw/network_fixes.csv
# Residence times of WFD lakes from HydroLAKES v1.0 (CC BY 4.0), for lake path 'residence' (scripts/make_lake_residence.py).
!data/raw/lake_residence.csv
# The same at spill-time flow (EA Hydrology daily mean flows, OGL v3.0), for lake path 'residence_spill' (scripts/make_lake_spill_ratio.py).
!data/raw/lake_residence_spill.csv
# Reasons for not achieving good status per water body, and each spot's water body (EA Catchment Data Explorer, OGL v3.0; scripts/make_rnags.py).
!data/raw/rnags.json
# Each overflow's dry-weather spill-days in a year (EA start/stop records, OGL v3.0): read by the page's note only, never the model (scripts/make_dry_weather_spills.py).
!data/raw/dry_weather_spills.csv
# Each spot's spill days upstream by month, 2021-2025 (EA start/stop records, OGL v3.0; Northumbrian, Wessex and United Utilities
# layers, CC BY 4.0): read by the page's history fold only, never the model (scripts/make_seasonal_spills.py).
!data/raw/seasonal_spills.json
